# Unity Object lookup APIs (Unity 6.5)

## Prefer

```csharp
// Single instance when order does not matter (usual case)
EventSystem es = Object.FindAnyObjectByType<EventSystem>();

// Multiple instances — no sort-mode argument
Camera[] cameras = Object.FindObjectsByType<Camera>();
```

If the file has `using System;`, qualify as `UnityEngine.Object.FindAnyObjectByType<T>()` / `UnityEngine.Object.FindObjectsByType<T>()` to avoid CS0104 (`Object` ambiguous with `System.Object`).

## Avoid (CS0618 / legacy)

```csharp
// ❌ Obsolete — relies on instance ID ordering
Object.FindFirstObjectByType<EventSystem>();

// ❌ Obsolete — FindObjectsSortMode parameter deprecated in Unity 6.5
Object.FindObjectsByType<Camera>(FindObjectsSortMode.None);
Object.FindObjectsByType<Camera>(FindObjectsSortMode.InstanceID);

// ❌ Legacy — do not use
Object.FindObjectOfType<EventSystem>();
Object.FindObjectsOfType<Camera>();
```

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| One object, order irrelevant | `FindAnyObjectByType<T>()` |
| All objects | `FindObjectsByType<T>()` with **no** `FindObjectsSortMode` argument |

# Object identity: EntityId (Unity 6.5)

Unity 6.5 replaces 32-bit `InstanceID` with the 64-bit `EntityId` struct. Obsolete InstanceID APIs are **compile errors** (CS0619).

## Prefer

```csharp
EntityId id = someObject.GetEntityId();
UnityEngine.Object obj = Resources.EntityIdToObject(id);
bool valid = Resources.EntityIdIsValid(id);
```

Store and pass `EntityId` as `EntityId` — including dictionary keys and method parameters.

## Avoid (CS0619 / unsafe)

```csharp
// ❌ Obsolete — compile error in Unity 6.5
int id = someObject.GetInstanceID();
Object obj = Resources.InstanceIDToObject(id);

// ❌ Do not truncate or fake an int identity from EntityId
int truncated = (int)someObject.GetEntityId();           // loses data
int hashAsId = someObject.GetEntityId().GetHashCode(); // not a unique object id

// ❌ Do not serialize EntityId via ToString / parse back as an int
```

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Object identity handle | `GetEntityId()` → store as `EntityId` |
| Id → object | `Resources.EntityIdToObject(EntityId)` |
| Validity | `Resources.EntityIdIsValid(EntityId)` |
| Non-identity int (e.g. NavMesh `avoidancePriority` 0–99) | Stable hash from **name** / designer index — **not** from `EntityId` |

# TextMesh Pro Essentials (UI text)

Creating `TextMeshProUGUI` / TMP text **requires** TMP Essential Resources under `Assets/TextMesh Pro/`. The package alone is not enough.

Before Editor setup scripts create TMP UI:

1. Check for `Assets/TextMesh Pro/Resources/TMP Settings.asset` (and a default font such as LiberationSans SDF).
2. If missing, import essentials via `TMP_PackageResourceImporter.ImportResources(true, false, false)` **or** stop with a beginner dialog telling the user to click **Import TMP Essentials** (skip Examples & Extras).
3. Never assume `TMP_Settings.defaultFontAsset` is non-null on a fresh project.

# TextMesh Pro wrapping (Unity 6 / current TMP)

## Prefer

```csharp
using TMPro;

tmp.textWrappingMode = TextWrappingModes.Normal;   // wrap (old enableWordWrapping = true)
tmp.textWrappingMode = TextWrappingModes.NoWrap;   // single line (old enableWordWrapping = false)
```

Other modes when needed: `PreserveWhitespace`, `PreserveWhitespaceNoWrap`.

## Avoid (CS0618)

```csharp
// ❌ Obsolete — use textWrappingMode instead
tmp.enableWordWrapping = true;
tmp.enableWordWrapping = false;
```
